# ouroboros#192: the VM sets EIGS_MATH_UNDERFLOW when a product or quotient
# of two NONZERO operands is exactly zero; the AOT's num_guard saw only the
# result and never set it, so math_flags read it clear (silent, rc 0).
# Mirrored at the multiply/divide emission, gated on the program reading
# math_flags. Controls: a real zero factor and exact cancellation must NOT
# flag; overflow still flags. (A product inside a FUNCTION does not set
# the flag on the pinned VM at all -- filed upstream; not pinned here.)
# EigenScript v0.46.0 removed `clear_math_flags`, and the flags are sticky,
# so the controls now run FIRST (each must leave the flag clear) and the
# multiply that must set it runs last; the divide half moved to
# t410_math_underflow_div.eigs, which needs its own clear process.
define uf() as:
    return (math_flags of null)["underflow"]
c is 3.0 * 0.0
print of [c, uf of null]
d is 5.0 - 5.0
print of [d, uf of null]
a is 1e-300 * 1e-300
print of [a, uf of null]
e is 1e300 * 1e300
print of [(math_flags of null)["overflow"], uf of null]
